node_modules
.next
*.log

# This repo's build context is its ROOT (see docker-compose.yml's
# frontend `context: .`), and the frontend Dockerfile does `COPY . .` —
# so without this line the ENTIRE backend/ tree (~7.5 MB of Python,
# fonts and subject artwork) is sent to the daemon and baked into the
# builder layer on every single frontend build. The frontend needs
# exactly none of it. backend/ has its own Dockerfile and its own
# context (`context: ./backend`), unaffected by this file.
backend/

# Depth-matters: Docker matches these against the path from the context
# root, so a bare ".env*" catches ./.env but NOT backend/.env — which is
# exactly the file carrying every real secret once start.sh has
# generated it on a server. "**/.env*" catches it at any depth. Kept
# alongside backend/ above rather than relying on it: if the ignore of
# backend/ is ever narrowed, this still holds the line.
.env*
**/.env*
!.env.production.example
!**/.env.example
